[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:46. Expensive and Uncomfortable]
[00:00.740]Passage 46 | 文章四十六
[00:02.515]Expensive and uncomfortable. | 昂贵而又不舒服。
[00:06.615]When a plane from London arrived at Sydney Airport, | 一架从伦敦飞来的飞机抵达悉尼机场时，
[00:11.485]workers began to unload a number of wooden boxes which contained clothing. | 工人们开始卸下一些装有衣服的木箱。
[00:17.375]No one could account for the fact that one of the boxes was extremely heavy. | 谁也搞不清其中一只箱子为什么特别重。
[00:24.360]It suddenly occurred to one of the workers to open up the box. | 一个工人突然想到把箱子打开。
[00:29.725]He was astonished at what he found. | 他被眼前发现的东西惊呆了。
[00:33.340]A man was lying in the box on top of a pile of woolen goods. | 一个男人躺在箱子里，身子压在一堆羊毛制品上面。
[00:39.425]He was so surprised at being discovered that he did not even try to run away. | 他因被发现而感到非常惊讶，甚至没想逃跑。
[00:46.395]After he was arrested, the man admitted hiding in the box before the plane left London. | 被捕后，这个男人承认在飞机离开伦敦前就藏在了箱子里。
[00:53.715]He had had a long and uncomfortable trip, | 他经历了一次漫长而不舒服的旅行，
[00:57.140]for he had been confined to the wooden box for over 10 hours. | 因为他被关在木箱里十多个小时了。
[01:03.110]The man was ordered to pay 345 pounds for the cost of the trip. | 这个男人被要求支付345英镑作为这次旅行的费用。
[01:10.130]The normal price of a ticket is 230 pounds. | 一张机票的正常价格是230英镑。